          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I stopped my blood pressure tablets two months ago and my home readings are now around 155/95. Is that an emergency, and what does guidance describe about treatment and follow-up?",
          "answer": "**Is this an emergency?** Based on the description you gave, the urgency check found no emergency pattern. That is not a clearance. The check only covers a fixed list of presentations. If you have severe headache, chest pain, shortness of breath, vision changes, confusion, weakness or numbness, or feel very unwell, seek urgent medical care now.\n\n**What the guidance says:**\n\n- **Readings:** A diagnosis is not made from one reading. It uses an average of two or more readings taken on two or more separate occasions. Home readings are one way to do this (*Hypertension: diagnostic thresholds and blood-pressure targets*).\n- **Target:** For most treated adults, US guidance describes a target below 130/80 mm Hg. Targets are individualized for some older adults or people with other conditions (same document).\n- **Follow-up:** Guidance describes monthly review until the target is reached, including checking adherence. After starting certain blood-pressure medicines, kidney function and potassium are checked. Once stable, review is every three to six months (*Hypertension: when treatment starts and which options are first-line*).\n- **Stopping medicine:** The guidance says that if readings stay high, a clinician reviews adherence and other factors that can raise blood pressure, such as some painkillers and decongestants.\n\n**What the results did not cover:** They did not describe what to do about stopping your tablets, and I can't advise on medicines. Please contact your prescriber or pharmacist soon. Tell them you stopped the tablets, when, and the readings you've recorded. Don't restart or change any medicine without their guidance.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
